course: dictionary
lesson: 1935
title: Praise, or trust in God's care
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which one you need. Commend is one of these. Its everyday meaning is to praise someone, especially officially or in public, as in a school report that says a child is commended for effort.
explain: The word can also mean to recommend something as good. In church it has a different meaning: to give someone into God's care. The vicar's words in a funeral are formal and old, and they sit beside words like thanks and remember, so «commend him to God» means trusting him to God, not praising him.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «The Church of England uses funeral words» tells you these words are solemn and religious. If you try praise in «commend him to God», it sounds odd, so the church meaning fits better.
fact: «Commend» means to praise someone or something, especially officially or in public.
fact: «Commend» can also mean to recommend something as good.
fact: In church, to «commend» someone to God means to entrust them to God's care.
fact: Phrases to know: highly commended, commended for bravery, commended for effort.
fact: You will often meet «commend» in formal places such as school reports, news stories, awards and funerals.
exercise: The newspaper said the firefighter was «commended for bravery». What does commended mean here? | Paid for a holiday | Criticised for being late | *Praised | Forgotten
exercise: In church, what does «to commend someone to God» mean? | To cook a meal for someone | To lose someone in a crowd | To throw a party | *To give someone into God's care
exercise: Mrs Patel wrote, «Sam is highly commended for effort.» What does highly commended suggest? | Sam was late for school | *Sam was praised very warmly | Sam lost his book | Sam is in trouble
test: «The judges commended the team for their teamwork.» What does commended mean here? | Ignored | Criticised | *Praised | Copied
test: The vicar says, «We commend him to God.» What is the vicar doing? | *Entrusting him to God's care | Asking for a loan | Telling him a joke | Giving thanks for the food
exam: The newspaper said the nurse was «commended for her courage». Which meaning fits best? | Stopped from working | Given a new uniform | Blamed for a mistake | *Praised for her courage
